Earnings Call Summary
Hims & Hers Health reported Q3 2026 revenue up 49% year-over-year to $890 mil=
lion, marking its second consecutive quarter of accelerating top-line growth.=
 Revenue excluded $18 million in deferred weight loss membership revenue, whi=
ch will be recognized in Q4 2026. Subscribership grew 13% year-over-year to 2=
.8 million users.
At a Glance
Hims & Hers Misses Financial Targets:
For Q3 2026, Hims & Hers Health reported an Adjusted EPS of -$0.14, missing t=
he estimated $0.154, and posted revenue of $890.37 million, which slightly mi=
ssed the estimated $892.77 million.
Subscribers Shrink Sequentially Despite Expansion:
Total subscribers grew 13% year-over-year to 2.8 million, but experienced a s=
equential decline of 100,000 users from the previous quarter due to a deliber=
ate pullback in domestic weight loss marketing.
Full-Year Guidance Cut for EBITDA:
The company narrowed its full-year 2026 revenue guidance to a range of $3.13 =
billion to $3.15 billion, but lowered its full-year Adjusted EBITDA forecast =
to $257 million to $277 million due to strategic international investments an=
d membership revenue deferrals.
Gross Margins Contract Under Pressure:
Gross margin dropped significantly to 57% from 74% in the year-ago period, pr=
imarily compressed by the scaling of lower-margin branded weight loss product=
s and expanding international operations.
Stock Plummets Post Earnings Report:
Following the earnings release, the company's stock experienced a sharp sello=
ff, tumbling approximately 17% as investors reacted negatively to the wider q=
uarterly net loss and declining margins.
International Business Run-Rate Surges High:
Rest of the World revenues surged 320.7% year-over-year to $233.3 million, pu=
tting the international business on track to surpass a $1 billion revenue run=
-rate in 2027.
