Earnings Call Summary
Aveanna Healthcare reported strong Q3 2026 results, with revenue increasing 1=
1.8% year-over-year to $695.5 million and adjusted EBITDA growing 25% to $100=
.1 million. Performance was driven by solid organic growth across all three o=
perating segments, improvements in clinical and financial outcomes, and conti=
nued operational efficiencies.
At a Glance
Aveanna Misses EPS, Beats Revenue Estimates:
Aveanna Healthcare reported Q3 2026 adjusted EPS of $0.2, missing the estimat=
ed $0.207, while its reported revenue of $695.54 million beat the consensus e=
stimate of $680.62 million.
Strong Volume and Segment Growth Achieved:
The company experienced an 11.8% year-over-year revenue increase driven by gr=
owth across all business lines, including a 15.6% jump in Home Health and Hos=
pice alongside 13 million hours of care provided in Private Duty Services.
Full Year 2026 Guidance Upwardly Revised:
Management increased its full-year 2026 outlook, now expecting total revenue =
to exceed $2.695 billion and adjusted EBITDA to surpass $374 million.
Preferred Payer Strategy Drives Efficiencies:
CEO Jeff Shaner noted that directing caregiver capacity toward preferred paye=
rs willing to offer enhanced reimbursement rates substantially improved hirin=
g, retention, and overall operational margins.
Strong Cash Generation Helps Deleveraging Goals:
Year-to-date free cash flow rose to $141.2 million, supporting the firm's str=
ategic goal of achieving sub-3x net leverage by 2027 despite carrying $1.52 b=
illion in total debt.
Shares Decline Despite Higher Outlook:
Despite beating revenue expectations and increasing full-year guidance, Avean=
na's shares fell 6.88% in early trading as investors weighed near-term season=
al headwinds against the quarterly operational beat.
